{
  "_id": "proverbs14",
  "book": {
    "_id": "proverbs",
    "title": "Proverbs",
    "titleShort": "Prov.",
    "titleOfficial": "",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 14,
    "summary": "Go from the presence of a foolish man—A true witness delivers souls—Righteousness exalts a nation.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Every wise woman buildeth her house: but the foolish plucketh it down with her hands.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Woman."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that walketh in his uprightness feareth the Lord: but he that is perverse in his ways despiseth him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the mouth of the foolish is a rod of pride: but the lips of the wise shall preserve them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Where no oxen are, the crib is clean: but much increase is by the strength of the ox.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A faithful witness will not lie: but a false witness will utter lies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A scorner seeketh wisdom, and findeth it not: but knowledge is easy unto him that understandeth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "Prov. 8:9; 15:14; 17:24; 2 Ne. 9:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Go from the presence of a foolish man, when thou perceivest not in him the lips of knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wisdom of the prudent is to understand his way: but the folly of fools is deceit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:30."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Deceit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Fools make a mock at sin: but among the righteous there is favour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "Ether 12:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The heart knoweth his own bitterness; and a stranger doth not intermeddle with his joy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The house of the wicked shall be overthrown: but the tabernacle of the upright shall flourish.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Matt. 7:27 (24–27)."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "HEB tent."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Isa. 55:8 (8–9)."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Prov. 15:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even in laughter the heart is sorrowful; and the end of that mirth is heaviness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Laughter."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Eccl. 2:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The backslider in heart shall be filled with his own ways: and a good man shall be satisfied from himself.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The simple believeth every word: but the prudent man looketh well to his going.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise man feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool rageth, and is confident.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "2 Ne. 4:34; Morm. 3:9; 4:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is soon angry dealeth foolishly: and a man of wicked devices is hated.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The simple inherit folly: but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "TG Knowledge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The evil bow before the good; and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The poor is hated even of his own neighbour: but the rich hath many friends.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "D&C 56:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "Prov. 19:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that despiseth his neighbour sinneth: but he that hath mercy on the poor, happy is he.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "D&C 52:40; 104:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "TG Happiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 85
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Do they not err that devise evil? but mercy and truth shall be to them that devise good.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips tendeth only to penury.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Labor; Work, Value of."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The crown of the wise is their riches: but the foolishness of fools is folly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Foolishness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 42
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A true witness delivereth souls: but a deceitful witness speaketh lies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 56
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the fear of the Lord is strong confidence: and his children shall have a place of refuge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 26
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fear of the Lord is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the multitude of people is the king’s honour: but in the want of people is the destruction of the prince.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 29
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Self-Mastery."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Prov. 15:18; D&C 60:14. TG Patience."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "IE quick-tempered. TG Haste; Rashness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 27
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "Deut. 24:14 (14–15); Prov. 17:5; Matt. 25:45; D&C 56:16. TG Oppression."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked is driven away in his wickedness: but the righteous hath hope in his death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Death of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wisdom resteth in the heart of him that hath understanding: but that which is in the midst of fools is made known.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Righteousness exalteth a nation: but sin is a reproach to any people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "4 Ne. 1:16 (15–17). TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The king’s favour is toward a wise servant: but his wrath is against him that causeth shame.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
